{
 "translation": "Committees were formed in every street and every neighborhood, and at first, they diligently started the program of 'resettlement' in business, 'resettlement' on land, and 'resettlement' in homes. But there was one program that no one paid attention to. That program was about abducted women, and its slogan was 'resettle them in hearts'. This program faced strong opposition from Narayan Bawa's temple and the conservative communities living around it. To put this program into action, a committee was established in the Mullah Shakur neighborhood near the temple, and Sundarlal Babu was elected its secretary by a majority of eleven votes. The lawyer sahib, the head of Chowki Kalan, and the old clerk, and other respected people of the neighborhood, thought that no one else could do that work with more dedication than Sundarlal. Perhaps this was because Sundarlal's own wife, Lajo Lajwanti, had been abducted.",
